WEBVTT

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:04.310
What in the world is that Servant?

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:08.360
She's Iskandar's primary confidante.

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:10.320
That's why I'm troubled.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:17.990
I don't recall seeing her
among those in Ionioi Hetairoi.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.700
One who accompanied
the King of Conquerors,

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.540
a comrade in arms
who shared his dream,

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:27.000
should be fighting alongside him
after death as a Heroic Spirit.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.380
And yet...

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.210
Waver!

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:34.470
Welcome back!

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:40.350
Just as you asked, I arranged
for the auction to be delayed!

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.190
Imperfections in the catalog,
delays in the train...

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:47.770
He attacked from every front.
He was on a rampage.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:52.690
As I needed to add extra funding, I wrung in
a deal to delay the auction as much as possible!

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.150
A habitual complainer...

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.530
They said they would push the start
to midnight tonight.

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:01.290
So, half a day left.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:07.420
Yes. Shishigou's report
is just like what I had Gray tell you.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.920
Oh no, thank you for the hard work.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:14.170
You may be recovering from illness, but I do
anticipate your active role in the situation.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.930
You're wondering if I'm enjoying this?

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:18.430
Of course I am!

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.410
We've already decided
that Karabo was the perpetrator, right?

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:03.700
It's not set in stone yet.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.120
And...

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.870
the perpetrator for this case
is clearly my enemy.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:11.080
The perpetrator for this case?

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:13.210
Do you mean the one who killed Trisha?

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:16.550
The one who stole the Relic from you?

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.010
The Master of that Heroic Spirit?

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:21.470
Without a doubt,
all three are the same person.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:26.850
I would like to ask you
for help once again.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:33.650
Hey, why do I have to do
something like that?

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.980
I hate all of you!

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:41.110
I hate people who look
like they were recognized for their efforts!

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:45.410
I hate self-conclusive people who think
they don't have to be recognized by others!

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.750
You look like you fit
into both of those categories!

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.960
You're the worst of the worst!
I detest you!

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.460
Sir isn't saying that—

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:54.710
What he does is no different!

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.880
Because you guys are trying
to stand up against her!

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:01.760
Looking at that makes me feel miserable!

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.380
Ms. Olga Marie...

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:05.340
You guys are up against Policies!

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:09.680
They only think of all of us as pawns!

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.310
I know that.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.810
Even then, with what's behind all that,

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:18.070
I will fight!

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:24.410
I hate more than anything how I can't
completely reject you guys and your ways.

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.070
You are courageous.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.460
Let me tell you an old story.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:42.300
I stole that Relic.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:47.140
Instead of training to build
my pathetic self up to confront my mentor,

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:50.930
I had the misconception that I could
have him recognize me with stolen powers.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:56.350
I didn't have courage,
like you do now,

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:01.320
to throw my own feelings
at the face of an adult.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:06.410
I am simply a survivor.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:09.700
It's not like I'm standing up
against anything.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.580
It's just harder for me to stay crouching.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:15.580
Sir...

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:17.580
This time,

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:20.590
I want to win for sure.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:25.260
Because the perpetrator for this case
ended up being my enemy,

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:28.430
I can't lose against him at any cost!

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:31.930
Don't you want to win, Olga Marie?

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.600
Don't you want to prove to the world

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:38.650
that you won't simply cry yourself to sleep

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:41.480
when someone murders your attendant?

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:45.070
You just called me "Olga Marie."

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:48.160
Not as "Animusphere"
or "the Lord's daughter."

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.160
That's right. I need you.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:57.620
Don't forget, Lord El-Melloi II,
this is a deal.

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.790
I can feel the exhaust
shaking my stomach!

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:05.970
American cars really are great!

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:11.930
More like, were you really sent here
by Reines, Mr. Shishigou?

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:17.730
Yeah, that's right! Can you finally tell us
why you pulled us out of our special lecture?

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:21.610
A moving car is a boundary
between the living world and the underworld.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.940
It creates a pseudo-enclosed space
both physically and spiritually.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:27.070
It should be okay now.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.070
That is your new assignment.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.870
I see. This truly is...

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:39.790
Yeah. This job is suited for us, Flat!

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:46.380
The Greater Grail of Fuyuki is useless?

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.380
Yes.

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:49.760
Dad had said that in the past.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:52.600
As far as I am aware,

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:55.640
that Greater Grail is genuine
no matter how you think about it.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.020
Otherwise,

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:59.690
it wouldn't be able
to summon Heroic Spirits.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:01.150
Like I would know.

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:05.360
That was my dad's conclusions
for calling off going to the Holy Grail War.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:08.860
Trisha was looking into
the Holy Grail War. It was because...

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:15.580
she wanted to know
why your father stopped loving you.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.410
Trisha did?

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:21.170
And chasing after your father's
source of information,

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:23.420
she was murdered.

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:29.420
It seems like illusions.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:31.970
You mean the Holy Grail War?

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:34.140
Everything.

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:36.560
Your Holy Grail War,

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:38.720
the Child of Einnashe,

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:42.310
this Mystic Eyes Collection Train,
memories of Trisha...

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:45.820
They all feel like scenery left behind.

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:49.780
The host has long since gone
walking yonder,

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:53.320
but the shadow is still left behind
in present time.

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:56.030
Why is everyone desperately holding on,

00:07:56.280 --> 00:08:00.830
knowing that there's only the shadow left?

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:03.540
It's like an afterimage.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:07.710
Oh, that's it.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:08.670
Sir?

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:12.510
You are truly the heir of Animusphere.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.090
Do those eyes have
a birds-eye view of the world?

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:19.270
Wh-What? Don't compliment me
all of a sudden!

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:23.350
Oh no, you're worthy
of praise as an individual.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:27.110
I need to contact someone.

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:28.940
I'll be right back.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:34.280
This is Luviagelita. Who is this?

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.410
<i>It's me.</i>

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:38.450
<i>I heard you've been assisting Reines.
I give my thanks.</i>

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.950
<i>It is all fine as I've been remunerated.</i>

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.830
<i>Or is this an additional request?</i>

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:48.790
It is. How did Lord Animusphere
get to know of the Holy Grail War?

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:50.500
Even in the Clock Tower,

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:54.010
a surprisingly few Mages
even noticed that event.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:57.680
<i>There are traces of someone
controlling the information.</i>

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:03.180
<i>Looking at how Adashino has been reacting,
I don't think it was Policies. However,</i>

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:07.190
there's no doubt that someone
got Animusphere moving.

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:11.190
And Trisha was investigating it
when she was killed.

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:13.570
You may have forgotten,

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:17.070
but I'm not a member of the El-Melloi Class.

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:20.990
I've simply hired you as a personal tutor.

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:26.620
When the Holy Grail War is over,
I promise to give you personal lectures.

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:29.790
<i>I'll make sure to wring out
all your secrets when you do.</i>

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:38.090
For us, the Edelfelt Family, to intervene
in conflict to make the greatest profit...

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:41.010
It's finally time to show
what we can really do!

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:48.060
<i>Bright.</i>

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:52.820
This is an artificial environmental
model created by Animusphere.

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:54.280
Is this enough?

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:55.070
Yeah.

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.530
With a Leyline map this accurate.

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:04.620
I see. I get it.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:08.120
It's only a matter of what order.

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:11.750
I finally caught you this time!

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:15.010
Why didn't I notice this?

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:17.840
This is a not a mystery at all!

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:22.890
Why Hephaestion was female or why
she wasn't in Ionioi Hetairoi are not the issues!

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:24.600
The question is...

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:28.850
why did that thing claim to be Hephaestion?

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.350
The whydunit.

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:32.110
This is not a case at all.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:35.190
This is an afterimage
of what once was a case.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:38.860
No, it's a remnant that sees
even less salvation than that.

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:41.120
What in the world are you talking about?

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:44.120
Now, the final part.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.120
Ms. Adashino had been hiding it,

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:48.500
but other than Trisha Fellows'
severed head,

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:52.250
wasn't there something else
hidden within the imaginary space?

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:04.890
This fell out along with Trisha's head.

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:07.140
This is what I saw!

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:09.890
As expected. Damn Adashino!

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:13.400
She removed it from her deduction
as the puzzle pieces wouldn't fit with this.

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:16.780
Will that become the key
to reaching the true perpetrator?

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:18.110
Yes.

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:23.240
The deductions made by Policies
will completely be overturned.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:36.050
<i>Everyone, we will begin
the Mystic Eyes Auction shortly.</i>

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:43.050
<i>Please head over to the Warehouse for
a Myriad of Mystic Eyeballs, the Pandemonium.</i>

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:46.060
Lord El-Melloi II's Case Files
｛Rail Zeppelin｝ Grace note

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:50.850
25 million dollars.

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:51.940
30 million dollars.

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:53.440
40 million dollars!

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:58.860
Sold for 40 million dollars.

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:03.860
Nothing less from an authority
on Mystic Eyes.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:06.620
She doesn't hold back
for notable Mystic Eyes.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:07.990
And lastly,

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:10.160
our main item for this auction!

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:15.170
These are the Jewel-class
Mystic Eyes of Transience.

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:20.420
We will start at 30 million dollars.

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:22.880
40 million.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:24.340
- 50 million!
- 70 million!

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:25.300
80 million!

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:26.350
90 million!

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:27.350
100 million!

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:30.520
Even a Picasso piece is worth that much.

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:34.650
If it's Jewel-class Mystic Eyes,
it won't end at this level.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:36.310
130 million.

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:39.860
Oh no, no, no!
Policies has to be joking about this!

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:41.610
I'm serious of course.

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:43.780
140 million.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:45.160
150 million.

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:46.570
160 million.

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:50.240
200 million!

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:53.830
230 million.

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:57.840
230 million. Going once!

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:02.630
Going twice!

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:04.970
240 million!

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:08.220
What's wrong?

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:10.810
I said, "240 million dollars."

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:12.060
Auctioneer,

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:15.350
I would like you to please keep going.

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:18.560
Well then...

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:20.270
Hold on!

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:22.740
This is heating up way too much!

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:25.200
Auctioneer, let us take a break!

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:28.660
Motion accepted.

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:33.580
What's the meaning of this, Waver?

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:39.540
You can't possibly get that much money
ready in your current state!

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:43.630
But you were about to stand down
at 230 million!

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:46.430
All things considered...

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:50.180
Though, that said,
I'm dubious of Yvette's wallet, too.

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:53.180
Then, how much can Policies spend?

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:55.640
They don't care how much they spend.

00:13:56.730 --> 00:14:00.270
Those Mystic Eyes are under
Policies' management now.

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:05.610
The money from the successful bid
isn't going to Karabo but to Policies.

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:09.780
They can pay hundreds of millions of dollars,
and it all goes back to them?

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:13.910
Of course, there are limits to how much money
Adashino can move at her discretion,

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:17.500
and some money will be taken as commission
so it won't make a clear profit.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.250
But it's a shrewd plan
suited to her nature.

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:24.000
And what are you after, Waver?

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:27.760
Will you seriously go against
how much funding Policies has?

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:31.140
The enemy probably didn't expect
the prices to go this high.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:34.310
He surely has to be concentrating
during the auction.

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:37.020
That's when I'll ready my trump card.

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:40.100
This is quite an expensive
diversion you've got here!

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:42.610
You could buy a stealth fighter with it!

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:46.990
Hey, Waver,

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:49.030
let me ask you again.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:51.990
Can you promise me
that this will be amusing?

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:55.580
Is this an act worthy of putting
a friend's financial ruin on the line?

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.080
Can you swear that it is?

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:01.540
I promise you it will surely be to your liking.

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:04.920
All right, then!

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:08.510
Oh, it's me. Yeah, me.

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:12.550
You know about the tuning machine
you've been wanting? No, I won't give it to you.

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:15.310
But if I use it as collateral,
how much can you dish out?

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:18.770
30 million dollars?
No, that's not gonna fly!

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:21.060
You should at least be able to go 70 million!

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:24.730
Well, I don't have much time,

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:27.570
so we can compromise,
and I'll settle for 50 million.

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:29.320
We'll go with that.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:34.830
Okay! You have 130 million extra now!
Will we be able to fight now?

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:39.660
By the way, Gray, Reines entrusted you
with a card, didn't she?

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:42.830
Oh, y-yes! This is it!

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:45.920
I don't want to add to my debt.

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:48.840
But with this, I can secure
another 30 million.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:52.010
What's left is my bank account
and hidden fortune.

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:54.300
Now, how far can we go?

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:57.100
This is getting really interesting!

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:10.780
Why do you go so far?

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:11.900
Look here.

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:17.410
I'm a brute who finds entertainment
when others are corrupted or fall from grace.

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:25.790
I've always been like this, even before I found out
I'm physically hindered from becoming a Mage.

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:28.300
However,

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:31.670
a brute has dignity of being a brute.

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:33.970
If you think it seems fun,

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:36.890
you need to properly and squarely bet
until the ultimate end

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.890
even if you're betting
your parents or your own self!

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:44.770
If you stay in a safe area
without doing so,

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:47.770
that is no longer a brute.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:52.280
You demote yourself
to simply being a cowardly chicken.

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:57.530
Now, we will resume from 240 million.

00:16:57.990 --> 00:16:59.030
250 million.

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:00.540
260 million.

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:02.200
280 million!

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:03.290
300 million.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:04.670
320 million.

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:06.250
330 million!

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:08.130
340 million.

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:09.420
350 million.

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:10.800
360 million!

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:12.550
370 million.

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:14.430
400 million!

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:16.300
410 million!

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:26.310
410 million. Going once!

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:30.570
420 million.

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.150
430 million!

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:34.070
460 million!

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:35.450
500 million!

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:47.500
Hold on a second!

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.340
We won't allow a second break.

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:52.130
There is something about Trisha Fellows' death

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:54.510
that I want out in the open.

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:58.050
Oh, what's the matter, Lord El-Melloi II?

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:00.640
Are you dissatisfied with my deduction?

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:02.680
The logic was full of holes,

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:04.810
but your deduction itself had no errors.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:06.690
That is why...

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:09.060
I would like you to look at this first!

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:11.730
You know...

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:15.070
I needed it to resolve the situation.

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.740
I took some liberties
to bring it out here.

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:21.240
Let's hear the great detective's
deductions, then.

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:24.450
Then,

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:28.750
allow me to clear things up, starting
with the serial murders from seven years ago.

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:33.750
In that case, all victims were beheaded,
and their heads were missing.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:37.680
Now, what do you think based on the situation?

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:41.390
That they are dead.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:42.390
Huh?

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:44.470
Come on now, Waver!

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:47.230
If there's no head,
of course they're all dead!

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:50.900
Then, what was the reason
Trisha Fellows hid her head?

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:53.070
It was a dying message, right?

00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:55.360
Yvette Lehmann gets a 3 out of 10.

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:57.530
She was a wielder of Mystic Eyes.

00:18:57.530 --> 00:19:01.450
Th-Then, the perpetrator tried
to take Trisha's Mystic Eyes from her?

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:05.870
But this train is the only way Mystic Eyes
can be extracted from a human corpse.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:08.870
No, the victims' heads were all taken.

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:10.710
They weren't necessarily dead.

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:13.210
"You are dead if your head
has been taken away."

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:14.960
That is in itself an assumption!

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:18.130
Trisha's head, after being severed,

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:19.260
was still alive!

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:25.010
Yes. A talented Mage can keep
someone alive with just the head.

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:29.140
That way, he could freely use Mystic Eyes
without transplanting them.

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:32.270
You simply need the heads
of the Mystic Eye wielders.

00:19:32.860 --> 00:19:35.230
Sir, are you saying
that the case seven years ago

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:39.030
were crimes to seize and use
Mystic Eyes at will?

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:40.820
That's my deduction.

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:42.280
Then,

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:44.160
why was Trisha killed?

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:47.620
She was investigating the case
from seven years ago.

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:50.460
If the perpetrator obtained
Mystic Eyes from every victim,

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:54.670
it should've been possible to obtain
information about the Holy Grail War.

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:58.550
That's why he tried to contact
Karabo and myself.

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:01.300
In other words, you aren't denying

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:05.430
that Karabo Frampton was the perpetrator
for the case seven years ago, right?

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:08.060
Ms. Adashino, are you familiar with this?

00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:15.560
It's what Trisha Fellows hid inside
the imaginary spell together with her head.

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:19.190
As vision is the oldest form of Magecraft,

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:22.700
Mystic Eyes have a myriad
of countermeasures.

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:26.280
For instance, using a lewd talisman
to block line of sight of the witness.

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:31.540
If the power of vision is strong,
it can even be reflected.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:34.210
A reversal of Mystic Eyes.

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:38.630
I see. I had foolishly forgotten
about that possibility.

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:41.970
You can manipulate Mystic Eyes
that aren't being controlled.

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:46.850
The reason why you hid this was to prevent
everyone from realizing that possibility.

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:50.520
Do you want to say that Karabo
was being manipulated by Trisha?

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:52.560
That's a jump in logic.

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:57.270
I'm saying that the possibility of a third party
intervening with Karabo's Mystic Eyes

00:20:57.270 --> 00:21:00.990
is intentionally lacking
from your deduction.

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:02.780
I see.

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.070
Indeed.

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:07.410
So, the perpetrator and mastermind
are separate, huh?

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:09.740
So, what happens from there?

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:13.620
Trisha, in her Premonition, predicted
that she would meet Karabo.

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:19.000
She boarded this train to gain the truth
about seven years ago from him.

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:19.880
And then?

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:22.510
And that was her mistake.

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:28.970
She lost her life by a blade from the past
that could not be prevented by Premonition.

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:34.690
Um, sir, are you saying that the true
perpetrator manipulated Karabo

00:21:34.690 --> 00:21:39.190
and committed this murder
as well as the ones seven years ago?

00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:46.450
There's just one person who can make
that possible and also has a motive.

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:50.580
So, who is it?

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:52.450
Oh, that?

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:55.120
This is the answer.

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:10.010
EPISODE 11: Rail Zeppelin 5/6
The Residual Image and Auctions
